L482: SPIRIT 2013 Checklist: Recommended items to address in a clinical trial protocol and
L483: related documents*
L484: **Section/item** **Item**
L485: **No**
L486: **Description**
L487: **Administrative information**
L488: Title 1 Descriptive title identifying the study design, population, interventions,
L489: and, if applicable, trial acronym
L490: Trial registration 2a Trial identifier and registry name. If not yet registered, name of
L491: intended registry
L492: 2b All items from the World Health Organization Trial Registration Data
L493: Set
L494: Protocol version 3 Date and version identifier
L495: Funding 4 Sources and types of financial, material, and other support
L496: Roles and
L497: responsibilities
L498: **Introduction**
L499: 5a Names, affiliations, and roles of protocol contributors
L500: 5b Name and contact information for the trial sponsor
L501: 5c Role of study sponsor and funders, if any, in study design; collection,
L502: management, analysis, and interpretation of data; writing of the report;
L503: and the decision to submit the report for publication, including whether
L504: they will have ultimate authority over any of these activities
L505: 5d Composition, roles, and responsibilities of the coordinating centre,
L506: steering committee, endpoint adjudication committee, data
L507: management team, and other individuals or groups overseeing the
L508: trial, if applicable (see Item 21a for data monitoring committee)
L509: Background and 6a Description of research question and justification for undertaking the
L510: rationale trial, including summary of relevant studies (published and
L511: unpublished) examining benefits and harms for each intervention
L512: 6b Explanation for choice of comparators
L513: Objectives 7 Specific objectives or hypotheses
L514: Trial design 8 Description of trial design including type of trial (eg, parallel group,
L515: crossover, factorial, single group), allocation ratio, and framework (eg,
L516: superiority, equivalence, noninferiority, exploratory)
L517: 1
L518: Apelland T _, et al. BMJ Open Sp Ex Med_ 2023; 9:e001541. doi: 10.1136/bmjsem-2023-001541
L519: BMJ Publishing Group Limited (BMJ) disclaims all liability and responsibility arising from any reliance
L520: Supplemental material placed on this supplemental material which has been supplied by the author(s) _BMJ Open Sp Ex Med_
L521: **Methods: Participants, interventions, and outcomes**
L522: Study setting 9 Description of study settings (eg, community clinic, academic hospital)
L523: and list of countries where data will be collected. Reference to where
L524: list of study sites can be obtained
L525: Eligibility criteria 10 Inclusion and exclusion criteria for participants. If applicable, eligibility
L526: criteria for study centres and individuals who will perform the
L527: interventions (eg, surgeons, psychotherapists)
L528: Interventions 11a Interventions for each group with sufficient detail to allow replication,
L529: including how and when they will be administered
L530: 11b Criteria for discontinuing or modifying allocated interventions for a
L531: given trial participant (eg, drug dose change in response to harms,
L532: participant request, or improving/worsening disease)
L533: 11c Strategies to improve adherence to intervention protocols, and any
L534: procedures for monitoring adherence (eg, drug tablet return,
L535: laboratory tests)
L536: 11d Relevant concomitant care and interventions that are permitted or
L537: prohibited during the trial
L538: Outcomes 12 Primary, secondary, and other outcomes, including the specific
L539: measurement variable (eg, systolic blood pressure), analysis metric
L540: (eg, change from baseline, final value, time to event), method of
L541: aggregation (eg, median, proportion), and time point for each
L542: outcome. Explanation of the clinical relevance of chosen efficacy and
L543: harm outcomes is strongly recommended
L544: Participant
L545: timeline
L546: 13 Time schedule of enrolment, interventions (including any run-ins and
L547: washouts), assessments, and visits for participants. A schematic
L548: diagram is highly recommended (see Figure)
L549: Sample size 14 Estimated number of participants needed to achieve study objectives
L550: and how it was determined, including clinical and statistical
L551: assumptions supporting any sample size calculations
L552: Recruitment 15 Strategies for achieving adequate participant enrolment to reach
L553: target sample size
L554: **Methods: Assignment of interventions (for controlled trials)**
L555: Allocation:
L556: Sequence
L557: generation
L558: 16a Method of generating the allocation sequence (eg, computergenerated random numbers), and list of any factors for stratification.
L559: To reduce predictability of a random sequence, details of any planned
L560: restriction (eg, blocking) should be provided in a separate document
L561: that is unavailable to those who enrol participants or assign
L562: interventions
L563: 2
L564: Apelland T _, et al. BMJ Open Sp Ex Med_ 2023; 9:e001541. doi: 10.1136/bmjsem-2023-001541
L565: BMJ Publishing Group Limited (BMJ) disclaims all liability and responsibility arising from any reliance
L566: Supplemental material placed on this supplemental material which has been supplied by the author(s) _BMJ Open Sp Ex Med_
L567: Allocation
L568: concealment
L569: mechanism
L570: 16b Mechanism of implementing the allocation sequence (eg, central
L571: telephone; sequentially numbered, opaque, sealed envelopes),
L572: describing any steps to conceal the sequence until interventions are
L573: assigned
L574: Implementation 16c Who will generate the allocation sequence, who will enrol participants,
L575: and who will assign participants to interventions
L576: Blinding
L577: (masking)
L578: 17a Who will be blinded after assignment to interventions (eg, trial
L579: participants, care providers, outcome assessors, data analysts), and
L580: how
L581: 17b If blinded, circumstances under which unblinding is permissible, and
L582: procedure for revealing a participant’s allocated intervention during
L583: the trial
L584: **Methods: Data collection, management, and analysis**
L585: Data collection
L586: methods
L587: Data
L588: management
L589: Statistical
L590: methods
L591: 18a Plans for assessment and collection of outcome, baseline, and other
L592: trial data, including any related processes to promote data quality (eg,
L593: duplicate measurements, training of assessors) and a description of
L594: study instruments (eg, questionnaires, laboratory tests) along with
L595: their reliability and validity, if known. Reference to where data
L596: collection forms can be found, if not in the protocol
L597: 18b Plans to promote participant retention and complete follow-up,
L598: including list of any outcome data to be collected for participants who
L599: discontinue or deviate from intervention protocols
L600: 19 Plans for data entry, coding, security, and storage, including any
L601: related processes to promote data quality (eg, double data entry;
L602: range checks for data values). Reference to where details of data
L603: management procedures can be found, if not in the protocol
L604: 20a Statistical methods for analysing primary and secondary outcomes.
L605: Reference to where other details of the statistical analysis plan can be
L606: found, if not in the protocol
L607: 20b Methods for any additional analyses (eg, subgroup and adjusted
L608: analyses)
L609: 20c Definition of analysis population relating to protocol non-adherence
L610: (eg, as randomised analysis), and any statistical methods to handle
L611: missing data (eg, multiple imputation)
L612: **Methods: Monitoring**
L613: Data monitoring 21a Composition of data monitoring committee (DMC); summary of its role
L614: and reporting structure; statement of whether it is independent from
L615: the sponsor and competing interests; and reference to where further
L616: details about its charter can be found, if not in the protocol.
L617: Alternatively, an explanation of why a DMC is not needed
L618: 3
L619: Apelland T _, et al. BMJ Open Sp Ex Med_ 2023; 9:e001541. doi: 10.1136/bmjsem-2023-001541
L620: BMJ Publishing Group Limited (BMJ) disclaims all liability and responsibility arising from any reliance
L621: Supplemental material placed on this supplemental material which has been supplied by the author(s) _BMJ Open Sp Ex Med_
L622: 21b Description of any interim analyses and stopping guidelines, including
L623: who will have access to these interim results and make the final
L624: decision to terminate the trial
L625: Harms 22 Plans for collecting, assessing, reporting, and managing solicited and
L626: spontaneously reported adverse events and other unintended effects
L627: of trial interventions or trial conduct
L628: Auditing 23 Frequency and procedures for auditing trial conduct, if any, and
L629: whether the process will be independent from investigators and the
L630: sponsor
L631: **Ethics and dissemination**
L632: Research ethics
L633: approval
L634: Protocol
L635: amendments
L636: 24 Plans for seeking research ethics committee/institutional review board
L637: (REC/IRB) approval
L638: 25 Plans for communicating important protocol modifications (eg,
L639: changes to eligibility criteria, outcomes, analyses) to relevant parties
L640: (eg, investigators, REC/IRBs, trial participants, trial registries, journals,
L641: regulators)
L642: Consent or assent 26a Who will obtain informed consent or assent from potential trial
L643: participants or authorised surrogates, and how (see Item 32)
L644: 26b Additional consent provisions for collection and use of participant data
L645: and biological specimens in ancillary studies, if applicable
L646: Confidentiality 27 How personal information about potential and enrolled participants will
L647: be collected, shared, and maintained in order to protect confidentiality
L648: before, during, and after the trial
L649: Declaration of
L650: interests
L651: 28 Financial and other competing interests for principal investigators for
L652: the overall trial and each study site
L653: Access to data 29 Statement of who will have access to the final trial dataset, and
L654: disclosure of contractual agreements that limit such access for
L655: investigators
L656: Ancillary and
L657: post-trial care
L658: 30 Provisions, if any, for ancillary and post-trial care, and for
L659: compensation to those who suffer harm from trial participation
L660: Dissemination 31a Plans for investigators and sponsor to communicate trial results to
L661: policy participants, healthcare professionals, the public, and other relevant
L662: groups (eg, via publication, reporting in results databases, or other
L663: data sharing arrangements), including any publication restrictions
L664: 31b Authorship eligibility guidelines and any intended use of professional
L665: writers
L666: 31c Plans, if any, for granting public access to the full protocol, participantlevel dataset, and statistical code
